# 11. Security Requirements

- Passwords must never be stored as plain text.
- JWT authentication must protect private APIs.
- Role-based permissions must be enforced on the backend.
- Every organization-specific operation must enforce organization-level data isolation.
- Users cannot approve requests assigned to other users unless explicitly authorized.
- Only authorized administrators can configure workflows.
- Approval history must preserve accountability.

