# 14. Definition of Success

FlowPilot's MVP will be considered functional when the following scenario works completely:

1. An organization registers.
2. Its owner creates a workflow with multiple approval stages.
3. An employee submits a request.
4. The first assigned approver receives the request.
5. The approver approves it.
6. The request automatically moves to the next stage.
7. The final approver approves it.
8. The request becomes APPROVED.
9. The employee can see the final status.
10. The complete approval history is available.

The same process must also support rejection at any approval stage.

